{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick-witted dialogue and intricate storytelling.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. he is a brilliant computer programmer, but he is also socially awkward and struggles to connect with others. after a painful breakup with his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but it also gets mark into trouble with the university administration. he is then approached by a group of wealthy students, including cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to help them create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees, but he soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it without the winklevoss brothers' knowledge.\n\nmeanwhile, mark meets eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield, who becomes his business partner and friend. eduardo is a member of the phoenix club, one of the most prestigious social clubs at harvard, and he helps mark to get funding for the site. however, as the site grows in popularity, mark and eduardo's relationship begins to deteriorate.\n\nthe film also explores the legal battles that mark faces as a result of his creation. the winklevoss brothers sue him for stealing their idea, and mark is forced to settle the lawsuit out of court. the movie also shows the impact that facebook has on mark's personal life, including his relationships with his friends and family.\n\none of the strengths of the film is its dialogue, which is quick-witted and engaging.